WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.645
Patrasche lay still in the grass ditch.

2
00:00:04.646 --> 00:00:09.716
His cruel master had left him and was now far away.

3
00:00:09.717 --> 00:00:15.036
The road was busy, and hundreds of people passed by.

4
00:00:15.037 --> 00:00:21.800
Some were on foot, and some rode horses.

5
00:00:21.801 --> 00:00:27.020
Some people saw him, but most did not even look.

6
00:00:27.021 --> 00:00:29.360
No one stopped.

7
00:00:29.361 --> 00:00:32.950
A dead dog was not worth a thought.

8
00:00:32.951 --> 00:00:39.063
After a while, a little old man who was bent and lame came by.

9
00:00:39.064 --> 00:00:42.570
A little boy walked with him.

10
00:00:42.571 --> 00:00:48.268
The old man looked at the dog with pity, and the little boy too.

11
00:00:48.269 --> 00:00:51.587
They knelt down beside the dog.

12
00:00:51.588 --> 00:00:57.565
With much effort, the old man lifted Patrasche out of the ditch.

13
00:00:57.566 --> 00:01:04.170
Then he and the boy carried Patrasche back home to their little hut.

14
00:01:04.171 --> 00:01:07.915
The old man's name was Jehan.

15
00:01:07.916 --> 00:01:12.671
When Jehan had turned eighty, his daughter had died.

16
00:01:12.672 --> 00:01:16.838
He was asked to look after her two-year-old son.

17
00:01:16.839 --> 00:01:25.768
The old man could barely support himself, but he took the little boy willingly.

18
00:01:25.769 --> 00:01:29.808
Jehan's grandson was named Nello.

19
00:01:29.809 --> 00:01:36.273
They lived at the edge of a small village in a small but clean mud hut.

20
00:01:36.274 --> 00:01:43.035
They kept a little garden where they grew beans and pumpkins and herbs.

21
00:01:43.036 --> 00:01:47.428
There were only two dozen houses in the village.

22
00:01:47.429 --> 00:01:53.043
Their walls were painted white and shone in the sun like snow.

23
00:01:53.044 --> 00:01:59.518
They had colorful red roofs and shutters of bright green or sky blue.

24
00:01:59.519 --> 00:02:04.313
In the center of the village stood a red windmill.

25
00:02:04.314 --> 00:02:10.585
Around Jehan's hut stretched flat pastures and fields of corn.

26
00:02:10.586 --> 00:02:15.333
A great canal ran through the village and the fields.

27
00:02:15.334 --> 00:02:23.790
On both sides of the canal, long lines of poplar trees bent their branches in the breeze.

28
00:02:23.791 --> 00:02:31.019
Across the fields, the distant town of Antwerp was just visible on the horizon.

29
00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:35.750
But the tall spire of the Antwerp cathedral stood out.

30
00:02:35.751 --> 00:02:44.616
It shone bright in the morning sun, and at dusk, its shadow stood out against the clouds.

31
00:02:44.617 --> 00:02:51.339
Jehan and Nello made Patrasche a little straw bed in the corner of their hut.

32
00:02:51.340 --> 00:02:55.379
He was very weak, but still alive.

33
00:02:55.380 --> 00:03:00.417
For many days, Patrasche lay there, not moving.

34
00:03:00.418 --> 00:03:06.825
At night, Nello stayed awake, listening anxiously to his breathing.

35
00:03:06.826 --> 00:03:11.336
Jehan could not give Patrasche much food.

36
00:03:11.337 --> 00:03:15.920
He barely had enough for himself and his grandson.

37
00:03:15.921 --> 00:03:19.854
In his youth, Jehan had been a soldier.

38
00:03:19.855 --> 00:03:23.760
But his leg had been injured during the war.

39
00:03:23.761 --> 00:03:30.928
This made it difficult for him to work, and he had been poor ever since.

40
00:03:30.929 --> 00:03:35.708
Some days, Jehan and Nello had nothing to eat.

41
00:03:35.709 --> 00:03:40.672
But even though their lives were hard, they were content.

42
00:03:40.673 --> 00:03:49.750
Jehan was very gentle and good to the boy, and the boy was beautiful, truthful, and kind.

43
00:03:49.751 --> 00:03:57.435
During Patrasche's long recovery, Nello and his grandfather grew very fond of him.

44
00:03:57.436 --> 00:04:04.740
Nello leaned his cheek against Patrasche's fur at night, and they both slept soundly.

45
00:04:04.741 --> 00:04:11.093
Patrasche became part of their little family.

46
00:04:11.094 --> 00:04:16.256
One day, Patrasche made a noise, a little bark.

47
00:04:16.257 --> 00:04:21.742
Jehan and Nello laughed and then wept with joy.

48
00:04:21.743 --> 00:04:29.309
Little Nello made a necklace of flowers for Patrasche and hugged him around his huge neck.

49
00:04:29.310 --> 00:04:32.991
Patrasche was getting better.

50
00:04:32.992 --> 00:04:38.858
A few weeks later, Patrasche's health and strength returned.

51
00:04:38.859 --> 00:04:44.390
He stood up, and his big brown eyes showed surprise.

52
00:04:44.391 --> 00:04:48.320
Nobody was hitting him or cursing him.

53
00:04:48.321 --> 00:04:52.270
He looked lovingly at Jehan and Nello.

54
00:04:52.271 --> 00:04:59.437
He owed them his life.

